            %a{:href => "#Thom54"}> Thom 54
            ) is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
            which assigns
            %strong asymptotic normal distance
            from the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direction+vector"} direction
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonality"} perpendicular
                to the submanifold, with respect to a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+framing"} normal framing
            %li
              %p
                asymptotically, regarding all points outside a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhood"} tubular neighbourhood
                as being
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} at infinity
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.12277.pdf#page=24"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/CohomotopyChargeAsymptoticDistanceII.jpg", :width => "630"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "Cohomotopy+charge#SatiSchreiber19"} SS 19
          %p
            For maximal codimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configurations of points
            %a{:href => "cohomotopy+charge#Salvatore01"} Salvatore 01
            following
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "cohomotopy+charge#Segal73"} Segal 73, Section 1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "cohomotopy+charge#Knudsen18"} Knudsen 18, p. 49
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "cohomotopy+charge#Kallel98"} Kallel 98
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+class"} homotopy class
            of the Thom collpase map may be regarded as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+charge"} Cohomotopy charge
            of the submanifolds, as measured in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy"} Cohomotopy
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology"} cohomology theory
          %p
            The PT collapse is a useful approximation to the would-be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+inverse"} left inverse
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} embedding of topological spaces
          %p
            As such, it is is used to define pushforward of
            = succeed "-classes" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Umkehr+maps"}> Umkehr maps
            ”). It also appears as the key step in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+theorem"} Thom's theorem
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#ComponentDefinitionInTopologicalSpaces Component definition in topological spaces
          %p
            All
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            in the following are taken to be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
          %p
            Consider
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i \colon X \hookrightarrow Y
          %p
            an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
          %p Write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi i
                      %mi X
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mi T
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_i X \coloneqq i^* T Y/ T X
                for the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Th
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi i
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th(N_i X)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
                of the normal bundle;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi i
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon N_i X \longrightarrow Y
                for any choice of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhood"} tubular neighbourhood
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          #CollapseMap.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong collapse map
              (or the
              = succeed ")" do
                %em Pontrjagin-Thom construction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              and the choice of tubular neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo −
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c_i
                    \\colon
                    Y
                    \\to
                    Y/(Y - f(N_i X))
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    Th(N_i X)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the first morphism is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              onto the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              and the second is the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
          #RefinedCollapseMap.num_defn
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Since in the construction of remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CollapseMap"}
              every point of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_i X
              is associated to a particular point of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo +
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Y
                    \\longrightarrow
                    X_+ \wedge Th(N_i X)
            %p
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
              (canonically regarded as a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with a base point adjoined.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Rudyak98"} Rudyak 98, p. 317
          #ForEmbeddingsIntoAnNSphere.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Of particular interest is the case where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              in the above is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi dim
                        %mi X
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{dim X + k}
              or rather its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} sphere
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi dim
                          %mi X
                          %mo +
                          %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{dim X + k}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney+embedding+theorem"} Whitney embedding theorem
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              there exists an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              such that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mi k
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{n+k} \to S^{n+k}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CollapseMap"}
              has the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{n+k} \longrightarrow Th(N_i X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Composing this further with the canonical map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi E
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_i X \longrightarrow E O(k) \underset{O(k)}{\times} \mathbb{R}^{k}
              to the universal vector bundle of rank
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              yields a map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{n+k} \longrightarrow M O(k)
            %p
              from to the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group+of+a+spectrum"} homotopy group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{k}(M O)
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+theorem"} Thom's theorem
              says that all elements in the homotopy groups of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O
              arise this way, and that they retain precisely the information of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
              of manifolds
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              In this case the refined Thom collapse map of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RefinedCollapseMap"}
              is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo +
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{n+k}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    X_+ \wedge Th(N_i X)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The refined map in example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ForEmbeddingsIntoAnNSphere"}
              lifts to a morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S} \longrightarrow \Sigma_+^\infty X \wedge \Sigma^{-n-k} Th(N_i X)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th(N_i X)
              now the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
              of the normal bundle.
            %p
              This morphism is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit of an adjunction
              which exhibits the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_+^\infty X
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dualizable object
              in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Σ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi k
                      %mi Th
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi i
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^{-n-k} Th(N_i X)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+duality"} Atiyah duality
              and at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-duality"} n-duality
          %p
            Equivalently, one may proceed as follows. For a framed manifold i.e. a manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^n
            with a chosen trivialization of the normal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_i (M^n)
            in some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^{n+r}
            one has
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mo +
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T N_i(M^n)\cong \Sigma^r(M^n_+)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mo +
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^n_+
            is the union of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^n
            with a disjoint base point. Identify a sphere
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n+r}
            with a one-point compactification
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi r
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^{n+r}\cup \{\infty\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi r
                  %mo →
                  %mi Th
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi i
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n+r}\to Th(N_i X)
            obtained by collapsing the complement of the interior of the unit disc bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(N_i M^n)
            to the point corresponding to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(N_i M^n)
            and by mapping each point of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(N_i M^n)
            to itself. Thus to a framed manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^n
            one associates the composition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi r
                  %mo →
                  %mi Th
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi i
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi r
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mo +
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^{n+r}\to Th(N_i X)\cong \Sigma^r M^n_+\to S^r
          %p
            and its homotopy class defines an element in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n+r}(S^r)
          %h3#AbstractDefinitionInTermsOfDuality Abstract definition in terms of duality
          %p
            The following is a more abstract description of Pontryagin-Thom collapse in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-module+bundles"} (∞,1)-module bundles
          #SpanierDualityOperation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi whe
                    %mi Top
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D \coloneqq (-)^\vee\circ \Sigma^\infty_+ \coloneqq L_{whe} Top \to \mathbb{S}Mod
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spanier-Whitehead+duality"} Spanier-Whitehead duality
              map which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              first to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
              and then that to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
              in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} (∞,1)-category of spectra
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#ABG11"}> ABG 11, def 10.3
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+manifold"} compact manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbb{R}^n
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
              and write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ν
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \to X^{\nu_n}
              for the classical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+collapse+map"} Pontryagin-Thom collapse map
              for this situation, and write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S} \to X^{-T X}
            %p
              for the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping"} looping
              map from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
              of the negative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+duality"} Atiyah duality
              produces an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X^{- T X} \simeq D X
            %p
              which identifies the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty_+ X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S} Mod
              and this constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi T
                                %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝕊
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi D
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo →
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; X^{- T X}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{S}
                    \&amp;\underset{D(X \to \ast)}{\to}&amp;
                    D X
                    }
            %p
              identifying the classical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+collapse+map"} Pontryagin-Thom collapse map
              with the abstract
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphism"} dual morphism
              construction of prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpanierDualityOperation"}
            %p
              More generally, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \hookrightarrow X
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+duality"} Atiyah duality
              identifies the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+collapse+maps"} Pontryagin-Thom collapse maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi T
                        %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S} \to X^{-T X} \to W^{- T W}
            %p
              with the abstract
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphisms"} dual morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                    %mi W
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S} \to D X \to D W
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#ABG11"}> ABG 11, prop. 10.5
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Given now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi CRing
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in CRing_\infty
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphism"} dual morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S} \to D X
              induces under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              a similar Pontryagin-Thom collapse map, but now not in
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-modules"} (∞,1)-modules
              but in
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-modules"} (∞,1)-modules
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝕊
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \to D X \otimes_{\mathbb{S}} E
                    \\,.
            %p
              The image of this under the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} cohomology
              functor produces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝕊
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [D X \otimes_{\mathbb{S}} E, E] \to E
                    \\,.
            %p
              If now one has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"}> orientation
              )
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝕊
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D X \otimes_{\mathbb{S}} E, E] \simeq [X,E]
              that identifies the cohomology of the dual object with the original cohomology, then together with produces the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Umkehr+map"} Umkehr map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝕊
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [X,E] \simeq [D X \otimes_{\mathbb{S}} E, E] \to E
            %p
              that pushes the
              = succeed "-cohomology" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to the
              = succeed "-cohomology" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \ast
              we start with a more general map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            %p
              More generally a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
              may not exists, but
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝕊
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D X \otimes_{\mathbb{S}} E, E]
              may still be equivalent to a
              = succeed "-variant" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,E]_{\chi}
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,E]
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi χ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma_X(\chi),E]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mi Line
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi E
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi \colon \Pi(X) \to E Line \hookrightarrow E Mod
              is an (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-bundle"}> flat
              )
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-module+bundle"} (∞,1)-module bundle
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \simeq \underset{\to}{\lim}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Thom+spectrum"} generalized Thom spectrum
              construction). In this case the above yields a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Umkehr+map"} twisted Umkehr map
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#ABG10"}> ABG 10, 9.1
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              all collapse maps for different choices of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhood"} tubular neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the fact that the space of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhood"} tubular neighbourhood
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
          %h3#relation_between_cohomotopy_and_cobordism Relation between cohomotopy and cobordism
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
